On Fri, 2007-12-21 at 09:41 -0600, Xavier Toth wrote:
> What's the difference between an AVC and a USER_AVC?

The audit system distinguishes between AVC messages generated by the
kernel (type=AVC) and ones generated by applications (type=USER_AVC).
So USER_AVCs are from userspace object managers like dbusd or X.

The send_msg permission is controlling whether the client process that
connected to dbusd (as identified by the scontext) is allowed to send a
message to the server process that registered the service on the bus (as
identified by the tcontext).  See the dbus man page.

